\ ==== random ====

\ RNG: deterministic from a seed (same seed -> same sequence), range-bounded,
\ and uniform. Serial use is fully reproducible, so the sequence is golden.
42 seed random . random . random . cr   \ a fixed sequence for seed 42
42 seed random . random . random . cr   \ reseeding reproduces it exactly
7 seed [: 10 random-int . :] 8 times cr \ eight draws, each in [0,10)
1 seed 0 [: random + :] 10000 times 10000 / . cr  \ mean over 10k draws ~ 0.5

\ bound must be positive
0 random-int
-3 random-int

clear

\ ==== sample ====

\ sample ( collection n with-replacement? -- array ): deterministic under a fixed seed.
\ Covers with/without replacement, full permutation, count 0, sets, empty,
\ non-numeric elements, and the error cases.
1 seed
[ 10 20 30 ] 6 true sample . cr          \ with replacement: repeats allowed, n may exceed size
[ 10 20 30 40 50 ] 3 false sample . cr   \ without replacement: distinct elements
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 4 false sample . cr          \ full permutation (n = size, no replacement)
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 0 true sample . cr           \ count 0 -> empty array
[< 7 8 9 >] 2 false sample . cr            \ from a set -> array of elements
[ "a" "b" "c" ] 4 true sample . cr       \ non-numeric elements, with replacement
[ ] 5 true sample . cr                   \ empty collection -> empty array

\ shuffle (lib): a full no-replacement draw; input untouched
[ 1 2 3 4 5 ] dup shuffle . cr
. cr                                     \ the source array is unchanged

\ resample (lib): a same-size draw with replacement; input untouched
[ 10 20 30 40 ] dup resample . cr
. cr                                     \ the source array is unchanged
[< 5 6 7 >] resample . cr                  \ from a set -> array of elements
[ ] resample . cr                        \ empty -> empty

\ error cases
[ 1 2 ] 5 false sample                   \ more than available, without replacement
[ 1 2 3 ] -1 true sample                 \ negative count
42 3 true sample                         \ argument is not a sequence

clear
